WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.417 --> 00:00:07.507
 ♪♪

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:11.678
Neil:
I didn't want to write an
unhappy marriage.

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:15.098
But all marriages involve
different kinds of tension 

00:00:15.098 --> 00:00:16.558
different kinds of compromise

00:00:16.558 --> 00:00:18.185
Neil:
different world views.

00:00:18.185 --> 00:00:23.482
Neil:
And so what I wanted to do was
look at the thematic fault-lines 

00:00:23.482 --> 00:00:25.901
Neil:
running through their
philosophies.

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:28.237
Let's be clear, it's not me,
it's you killing this woman!

00:00:28.237 --> 00:00:29.279
What do you want me to say?

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:33.116
Neil:
There's some level of assumption
that Margot is

00:00:33.116 --> 00:00:34.368
Neil:
in some way along for the ride.

00:00:34.368 --> 00:00:35.035
(Gunshot)

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:37.246
Neil:
In that moment in this
episode...

00:00:37.246 --> 00:00:38.497
(Heavy breathing)

00:00:38.497 --> 00:00:42.584
Neil:
.... we get the first real solid
glimmer

00:00:42.584 --> 00:00:46.838
that things might be otherwise.

00:00:46.838 --> 00:00:48.507
Melissa:
When you get told something

00:00:48.507 --> 00:00:50.592
there's a gun at the back
wife's head

00:00:50.592 --> 00:00:53.720
Melissa:
and you actually don't care

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.681
Melissa:
well that's what she thinks 
Allie was going through.

00:00:55.681 --> 00:00:57.015
Melissa:
She's had enough.

00:00:57.015 --> 00:00:59.393
Melissa:
That's when she realizes that
she's gotta take the kids.

00:00:59.393 --> 00:01:00.644
Melissa:
And life with Allie is not worth
it. 

00:01:01.353 --> 00:01:03.689
Margot:
You promise and promise but
never deliver. 

00:01:04.189 --> 00:01:05.482
Margot:
That's my fault.

00:01:06.149 --> 00:01:07.734
But that's not happening
anymore.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.361
♪♪

00:01:09.361 --> 00:01:10.779
That's over.

00:01:11.655 --> 00:01:13.490
Rupert:
There's always a compelling
story to be told

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:15.742
when you're telling the story of
people who love each other 

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:17.452
Rupert:
but find it hard to coexist.

00:01:17.452 --> 00:01:20.497
Rupert:
And when that actually then gets
to the stakes of Life and Death.

00:01:20.497 --> 00:01:21.873
Rupert:
I think it makes for
great drama.

00:01:22.499 --> 00:01:25.335
For Margot and Allie I said
"Well is this a romantic
couple?"

00:01:25.335 --> 00:01:28.171
We've had long conversations of
whether they are even in love
anymore.

00:01:28.171 --> 00:01:31.300
Justin:
For so long it's been
function of just survival.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:35.929
They both take turns using
different limbs to try and wrap
their arms around their family.

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:38.098
Justin:
And I think they have an
intuitive knowledge

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:39.099
Justin:
on how to do it.

00:01:39.808 --> 00:01:42.853
Margot's main priority is the
family.

00:01:42.853 --> 00:01:46.273
Gabriel:
And Melissa, I think, really
brings out the motherly aspect.

00:01:46.273 --> 00:01:49.067
She's like that on set all the
time, she's just very kind and
caring.

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:50.485
Whispering:
Don't! Get down!

00:01:50.485 --> 00:01:51.486
The cops are coming.

00:01:51.486 --> 00:01:54.448
Rupert:
Justin and Melissa, they created
a real bond.

00:01:54.448 --> 00:01:56.700
You know they really
work together immensely well.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.702
Melissa:
Working with Justin is
just incredible.

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:01.872
He's so great to just like throw
ideas off.

00:02:01.872 --> 00:02:04.082
Logan:
He did a really great job
at just making

00:02:04.082 --> 00:02:08.128
everyone multi-dimensional so
that there was a lot of just
subtext going on.

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:10.630
And there would be a look between
Allie and Margot

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:12.382
Melissa:
and you know, without even
speaking, that the two

00:02:12.382 --> 00:02:15.052
Melissa:
of them know exactly what to do
in order to get them 

00:02:15.052 --> 00:02:16.428
Melissa:
out of the situation.

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:17.721
Margot:
Lock yourself in the bathroom.

00:02:18.221 --> 00:02:21.767
Their bond and their love is
really through the conduit of
their children.

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:24.770
Justin:
And I wonder if anything ever,
God forbid, happened to their 

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:26.772
Justin:
children whether they would even
stay together

00:02:26.772 --> 00:02:28.565
Justin:
or whether there would be a
purpose to.

00:02:28.565 --> 00:02:34.029
♪♪

